---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import GlowLineSeparator from '@/components/ui/separator/GlowLineSeparator.astro';
const pageTitle = 'About Me';
const pageDescription = 'Learn more about my background in product management, analytics, and growth.';
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} pubDate={new Date()} showHeader={false}>
  <p>
    I’m Abhishek Saxena — a Product Manager with 9+ years at the intersection of data and product. I’ve been promoted twice in two years: from Senior Product Analyst to APM (Jan 2025), then to PM (Jan 2026), each time by taking full ownership of ambiguous problems and shipping measurable outcomes.
  </p>
  <p>
    The move from analyst to PM wasn’t just a title change — it was a shift in ownership. I went from answering questions with data to deciding which questions were worth asking. At Glance, I own ambiguous product problems end-to-end: defining what the real problem is, shaping the solution, running the experiment, and making the call on what comes next. The Bundles arc — from a session continuity hypothesis to 8 shipped experiments across format, discoverability, and video — is the clearest example of that full-loop ownership, all within a single product area.
  </p>
  <p>
    AI is part of how I think, not just how I work. I start with it for PRD writing — not to auto-generate specs, but to ask sharper questions, stress-test assumptions, and brainstorm edge cases before a single meeting. I use it to prototype ideas fast, understand codebase architecture and technical system design, and keep engineering constraints visible when writing requirements. That last part matters: when I understand how the system actually works, I can give engineers cleaner, constraint-aware specs and move from problem to shipped feature at a faster rate. Building this portfolio with Claude Code is a small example of the same habit — understand the system, define what needs to happen, then build.
  </p>
  <p>
    My foundation is deep data fluency: advanced SQL (BigQuery, PostgreSQL), Python (Pandas), A/B testing, funnel analysis, cohort modeling, and instrumentation design. I’ve built dashboards from scratch (Fast Card funnel, Novo Master, SHP 3P), run war-room analyses on 6-month datasets, and designed tracking requirements before a single line of code was written.
  </p>
  <p>
    Before Glance, I drove 3.5× revenue impact at Chingari (Web3), built analytics for a $25Mn ARR gaming platform at Gameberry Labs, reduced last-mile logistics costs at Shadowfax, and consulted on AI/ML projects at Infosys. I thrive wherever the problem is hard, the data is messy, and the stakes are real.
  </p>

  <GlowLineSeparator />

</Layout>
